  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Humorous, teasing couplet song of Slavonia, Baranja and Srijem in eastern Croatia, improvised at weddings, harvest work and village feasts and inscribed by UNESCO on its Representative List as bećarac singing and playing from Eastern Croatia. A leading singer calls out a two-line decasyllabic verse and the group joins on the repeat, accompanied by a tamburica band of small lead and middle lutes, chord-strumming bugarija and berde bass.",
